{"word": "barely", "source": "freedictionaryapi", "data": {"word": "barely", "entries": [{"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "adverb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈbɛə(ɹ).li/", "tags": ["UK"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈbɛɹ.li/", "tags": ["US"]}], "forms": [{"word": "more barely", "tags": ["comparative"]}, {"word": "most barely", "tags": ["superlative"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "(not comparable, degree) By a small margin.", "tags": ["not comparable"], "examples": ["I barely completed my homework. However, I got a score of 5 for it.", "1925, Walter Anthony and Tom Reed (titles), Rupert Julian (director), The Phantom of the Opera, silent movie\n‘It is barely possible you may hear of a ghost, a Phantom of the Opera!’"], "quotes": [{"text": "It becomes, therefore, no inconsiderable part of science barely to know the different operations of mind,", "reference": "1748, [David Hume], Philosophical Essays Concerning Human Understanding, London: […] A[ndrew] Millar, […], →OCLC, part VIII:"}, {"text": "As our train to Paris dashed through the labyrynthine flyovers at Porchefontaine, barely a mile from Versailles, the 75 m.p.h. limit was already almost attained.", "reference": "1961 November, H. G. Ellison, P. G. Barlow, “Journey through France: Part One”, in Trains Illustrated, page 670:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "بِٱلْكَاد"}, {"language": {"code": "acw", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "يا دوب"}, {"language": {"code": "acw", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "ياالله"}, {"language": {"code": "ajp", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "بالكاد"}, {"language": {"code": "ajp", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "أنجق"}, {"language": {"code": "hy", "name": "Armenian"}, "word": "հազիվ"}, {"language": {"code": "be", "name": "Belarusian"}, "word": "ледзь"}, {"language": {"code": "be", "name": "Belarusian"}, "word": "ле́дзьве"}, {"language": {"code": "be", "name": "Belarusian"}, "wor